Subject: [202605] Recognize the FSF019 PSU's observed F2B* airflow label

Both FSF019-611 PSUs on the AS7326 test switch return the literal F2B* from
psu_fan_dir. The existing lookup accepts only F2B, so health reports an
incorrect mismatch with EXHAUST chassis fans after target checks are skipped.
Map this exact observed label to the existing EXHAUST value. Keep unknown
labels unchanged so genuine mismatches and unsupported data stay visible.
Edgecore's custom driver independently classifies FSF019 as F2B:
https://github.com/edge-core/sonic-buildimage/blob/d39662e996c0e8748c9b96ad88dc5f5f524e8048/platform/broadcom/sonic-platform-modules-accton/as7326-56x/modules/pddf_custom_psu.c
No fan direction or status check is disabled; no hardware registers change.
Verified upstream: 5ef9e45ccf7f004fb07bf3f9be2f471cf00573bf.

--- a/device/accton/x86_64-accton_as7326_56x-r0/pddf/pd-plugin.json
+++ b/device/accton/x86_64-accton_as7326_56x-r0/pddf/pd-plugin.json
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@
         {
             "i2c":
             {
-                "valmap": { "F2B":"EXHAUST", "B2F":"INTAKE" }
+                "valmap": { "F2B":"EXHAUST", "F2B*":"EXHAUST", "B2F":"INTAKE" }
             }
         },
 
